      "datePublished": "2026-05",
      "version": "V.05",
      "license": "CC-BY-4.0",
      "abstract": "Foundational work proposing that commitment, operationalized as the identity-bearing content of a linguistic signal, admits formal treatment as a conserved invariant under lossy transformation, recursive self-application, and compression. V.05 formalizes the conservation claim, introduces MO§ES™ as enforcement architecture, and integrates the EXP-001 through EXP-007 experimental record.",
      "keywords": [
        "Commitment conservation",
        "semantic information theory",
        "transformation fidelity",
        "recursive stability",
        "MO§ES™",
        "governance architecture"
      ],
